Imply MOZ_APP_VENDOR=Pyxis and MOZ_APP_BASENAME=Vela in browser configure defaults so generated application metadata (application.ini, XRE sAppData, and GTK application name) reports Pyxis Vela instead of Mozilla Firefox.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
index e8b401a7dfb2..c92b5c91594e 100644
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 
-imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Mozilla")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Pyxis")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_BASENAME", "Vela")
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
